Build a React single-file component (JSX) — an AI-powered JMX Script Generator 
for UI application load testing.

## FUNCTIONALITY
- Text area for the user to describe a UI flow 
  (e.g., "Login → Browse Products → Add to Cart → Checkout")
- Input fields for: Base URL, Virtual Users, Ramp-Up (seconds), Loop Count
- Quick example buttons that auto-fill the flow text area
- "Generate" button that calls the Anthropic Claude API 
  (POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages)
- Display the returned JMX XML in a syntax-highlighted code block
- Copy to clipboard and Download as .jmx buttons

## API CALL
Model: claude-sonnet-4-20250514
Max tokens: 4000
System prompt: You are a JMeter JMX expert. Output ONLY raw valid XML — 
no markdown, no explanation. Generate a complete JMX with:
ThreadGroup using the provided users/ramp-up/loops, HTTP Request Defaults 
with the base URL, Cookie Manager, Cache Manager, one HTTP Sampler per step 
(named "01 - Step Name"), GaussianRandomTimer between steps (1000ms mean), 
Response Assertions (HTTP 200), and a Summary Report listener.

## UI / DESIGN
Dark theme — background #0a0e1a, accent color #00ffaa (green), 
secondary accent #0099ff (blue)
Font: IBM Plex Mono (import from Google Fonts)
Two tabs: "Configure" and "Output"
Configure tab: flow textarea + 4 parameter inputs + generate button
Output tab: action bar (line count, Copy, Download buttons) + 
  styled code viewer with fake macOS window chrome (red/yellow/green dots) 
  + a "How to use" tip box
Loading state: spinner with animated status text
Subtle CSS grid background overlay (3% opacity green lines, 40px spacing)
All animations via CSS keyframes (spin, pulse)

## TECH CONSTRAINTS
- Single .jsx file, no external dependencies beyond React + Tailwind core utils
- Use useState, useRef hooks only
- No <form> tags — use onClick/onChange handlers
- Custom scrollbar styling via CSS
- Syntax highlight the XML output using dangerouslySetInnerHTML with 
  regex-based coloring (tags in blue #0099ff, strings in green #00ffaa, 
  comments in gray #475569)
